{"id": "EUVD-2026-108320", "enisaUuid": "8cae6898-a056-344a-b214-ab1bf3ffe49d", "description": "Wasmtime before 36.0.16, 37.0.0 before 48.0.3, and 49.0.0 before 49.0.1 does not adequately account for host allocations when lifting guest values through the dynamically-typed Val API, bypassing the hostcall fuel limit. A malicious WebAssembly guest can return crafted values that allocate at least ~100x more host memory than tracked, causing denial of service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T19:13:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T19:13:55", "baseScore": 1.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:A/AC:H/AT:P/PR:L/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/security/advisories/GHSA-jqpg-j7w6-42pr", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/wasmtime-before-36.0.16-37.0.0-before-48.0.3-and-49.0.0-before-49.0.1-denial-of-service-via-val-api"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-115389", "GHSA-3g9q-2gmg-4cvp"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "95a94a3c-2b74-35a5-aade-813437466228", "product": {"name": "wasmtime", "vendor": {"name": "bytecodealliance"}}, "product_version": "37.0.0 <48.0.3"}, {"id": "9bab3dcc-4822-3498-b88b-a3d08380b965", "product": {"name": "wasmtime", "vendor": {"name": "bytecodealliance"}}, "product_version": "0 <36.0.16"}, {"id": "d91b8e1e-8c29-34e2-a1f9-289e6987bb03", "product": {"name": "wasmtime", "vendor": {"name": "bytecodealliance"}}, "product_version": "49.0.0 <49.0.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c67c4fe5-15cb-3a04-825f-1f28789a7629", "vendor": {"name": "bytecodealliance"}}], "isExploited": false}